  "title": "SyncRequestProcessor ACK written before the NEWLEADER ACK is consumed as the NEWLEADER ACK",
  "cause": "The update starts the learner pipeline (startupWithoutServing) before the learner thread writes the NEWLEADER ACK, so a forced proposal's ACK can be the first packet LearnerHandler reads after NEWLEADER.",
  "trigger": "DIFF sync with at least one proposal; the learner thread is delayed between logRequest and the NEWLEADER ACK write (GC pause, preemption, or a large DIFF batch).",
  "consequence": "Leader.waitForNewLeaderAck discards the ACK as from a different epoch; the re-elected leader fails to establish its epoch and times out, and an established leader loses that proposal ACK.",
  "sites": [
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/Learner.java:751-760",
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/LearnerHandler.java:609-623",
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/Leader.java:1547-1588"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "LearnerNewLeader",
    "FsyncOne",
    "LearnerAckNewLeader",
    "LeaderReadNewLeaderAck"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "NewLeaderAckFirst"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "LearnerHandler treats the first ACK after NEWLEADER as the NEWLEADER ACK and waitForNewLeaderAck ignores a mismatching zxid.",
    "SyncRequestProcessor and the learner thread share the learner output stream."
  ],
